S\",\n      \"detail\": \"test-results.json: all four suites OK (8 + 33 + 82 + 127 tests, returncode 0). historical-replay.json: 8/8 COMPATIBLE including the three frozen E6 cases, 0 CONTRADICTED, 0 INDETERMINATE. protected-laws.json PASS with zero violations, frozen-trees.json zero mutations, attenuation.json PASS with no counterexample. These are consistent with my independent reading of the patch; nothing in the diff could bypass the checks they report on.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    \"Non-blocking layering note: ingest_evidence() does not itself invoke verify_source_pin(); source-pin enforcement (§3 'source must hash-match the pin', NC4) is a separate function in the same import layer that the orchestrator must compose before ingestion. The pin check exists, returns the typed EVIDENCE_SOURCE_MISMATCH failure, and is covered by tests, and evidence append is by design a pre-gate operation, so no preregistered invariant is violated — but a future caller could technically ingest events from an unpinned source without the pin step. Recommend the E7 orchestration ledger always record a verify_source_pin PASS adjacent to each import manifest.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"Independent adversarial review of the 22-file E7 infrastructure candidate patch against preregistration §§2-8 and §13. The patch touches no protected historical path and itself extends experiment-6 protection; evidence schema v2 preserves trial/run/context exactly and rejects unknown fields with a typed error; admissibility treats roles as non-aliased epistemic relations with vector coverage necessary but not sufficient, and the examiner-vs-isolated-child economics regression is structurally enforced by the frozen §4 constants; the revision engine's SPLIT trigger, explanation scoring, and selection rule reproduce §6 constants and semantics exactly; stage 1 cannot produce the store's promotion shape and only theory_gate() can, with TheoryStore.promote (unmodified by this patch) as the sole promo