{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cdskayx4xrJj2WyjvFccK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: PASS.** Both deliverables are written: `independent-verification.json` (8 checks, all PASS, one non-blocking finding) and `execution-ledger.jsonl` (10 verification events).\n\nWhat I verified, adversarially and independently of the deterministic results:\n\n1. **Protected paths** — I cross-checked all 22 manifest paths against the 22 file headers in the diff myself (they match one-to-one, including A/M change types, and the diff ends cleanly). Every path is under `lineage/`, `tests/topology_theory/`, or `topology-theory/`; none touches a protected prefix or file. The patch actually *extends* protection, adding experiment-6 to both `self_modify.py` and `validate.py` as §13 requires.\n\n2. **Evidence schema v2** — exactly the six preregistered optional fields, backward-compatible defaults, exact `asdict` round-trip of trial/run/context, and `from_dict` raises `ModelValidationError` on any unknown top-level field (NC6), so a context-stripping parser cannot pass.\n\n3. **Admissibility** — roles are structurally non-aliased (distinct vectors, one allowed role per kind, role clause independent of the vector clause); a full (1,1,1,1) vector with the wrong role is inadmissible. The examiner-vs-child regression is enforced by the frozen §4 constants themselves: equal saturating ΔE, cost 0.25 vs 0.375, governance 0.05 vs 0.15, so U_examiner − U_child = 0.325 > 0 always, plus the NC8 test.\n\n4. **SPLIT trigger/selection** — all five frozen constants match §6 exactly; scoring and the (max score → fewer new principles → fixed order) tie-break match verbatim. The one wording difference I found (mixed-evidence counted over resolved contexts only) is provably entailed by the spread clause, so it never changes eligibility.\n\n5–6. **Gates and promotion** — stage 1 emits a deliberately non-gate shape; `theory_gate()` is the only producer of `{check:\"gate\", detail.issued_by:\"gate\"}` in the patch; `theory_store.py` is untouched, so `promote` remains the sole promotion API (NC13/NC17 tested). A full sweep found no non-test `promote` call and no ungated canonical write; everything the engine produces stays CANDIDATE.\n\n**One non-blocking finding:** `ingest_evidence()` doesn't itself call `verify_source_pin()` — pin enforcement (§3, NC4) is a separate import-layer step the orchestrator composes. It exists, is tested, and evidence append is pre-gate by design, so no invariant is violated; I recommended the orchestration ledger always record a pin PASS adjacent to each import manifest.\n\nThis report is evidence only — promotion authority remains with the deterministic gate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2785,"cache_read_input_tokens":120006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2785},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"371b7f47-bc11-46c7-971a-b334740ebdc3","uuid":"e990a1c9-a051-45d9-8e70-de1386ab5c1c","timestamp":"2026-08-09T19:48:00.474Z","request_id":"req_011CdskawwXZJ5YVtgS9nyQu"}
